od a year ago, primarily reflecting a year-over-year decrease in organic revenue (excluding contributions from acquired companies and foreign exchange translation) of $66.1 million or 9.1%, partially offset by the positive impact of foreign exchange translation. Revenues generated from construction contracts decreased 19.2% or $77.2 million from the prior period primarily due to lower Order Backlog entering the period. Revenues from services increased 6.1% or $10.3 million, primarily due to organic revenue growth on higher Order Backlog entering the period and the positive impact of foreign exchange translation. Revenues from the sale of goods increased 2.7% or $4.2 million, which included a positive impact from foreign exchange translation. Organic revenue is a non-IFRS financial measure - see \"Non IFRS and Other Financial Measures.\"\n"}
{"page": 16, "text": "By market, revenues generated in life sciences decreased $18.7 million or 5.0% year-over-year. This was primarily due to timing of both customer capital allocation as well as project execution. Revenues in industrial & consumer decreased $41.8 million or 23.5% compared to the prior year as a result of lower activity in certain legacy industrial applications, as the Company continues to reposition its capabilities towards other strategic areas. Revenues generated in food & beverage decreased $25.2 million or 20.2% from the corresponding period last year due to lower Order Backlog entering the period, in\n11\naddition to timing of project execution. Revenues in energy increased $23.0 million or 45.1% year-over-year primarily related to execution of nuclear projects.\nRevenues for the six months ended September 27, 2026 were 7.2% or $105.7 million lower than in the prior year. On an adjusted basis, revenues were 6.9% or $101.1 million lower than the prior year, primarily reflecting a decrease in organic revenue (excluding contributions from acquired companies and foreign exchange translation) of $113.5 million or 7.7%, partially offset by a 0.8% positive impact of foreign exchange translation. Revenues generated from construction contracts decreased 16.4% or $134.9 million primarily due to lower Order Backlog entering the year. Revenues from services increased 8.7% or $29.0 million primarily due to organic revenue growth on higher Order Backlog entering the period and the positive impact of foreign exchange translation. Revenues from the sale of goods increased 1.6% or $4.8 million, which included a positive impact from foreign exchange translation.\nBy market, revenues in the first six months of fiscal 2027 from life sciences decreased $51.6 million or 6.9% over the prior period primarily due to timing of both customer capital allocation and project execution. Revenues in industrial & consumer decreased $50.4 million or 13.9%, primarily as a result of lower activity in certain legacy industrial applications. Revenues generated in food & beverage decreased $46.6 million or 17.7% from the prior period due to lower Order Backlog entering the period in addition to timing of project execution. Revenues in energy increased $47.5 million or 55.0% over the prior period due to organic revenue growth on higher Order Backlog entering the fiscal year, including execution of nuclear projects.\n"}
{"page": 17, "text": "Cost of revenues. At $476.3 million, second quarter of fiscal 2027 cost of revenues decreased by $34.3 million, or 6.7%, compared to the corresponding period a year ago, primarily due to lower revenues. Second quarter fiscal 2027 gross margin was 28.5% (or 28.6% on adjusted revenues and excluding cost of revenues from other reorganization-related costs of $0.9 million), compared to 29.9% in the corresponding period a year ago. The year-over-year decrease in gross margin on adjusted revenues excluding adjusting items was 131 basis points, primarily due to the impact of lower revenue volumes.\nYear-to-date gross margin was 27.9% (or 29.3% on adjusted revenues and excluding cost of revenues of $2.3 million from the transportation reorganization, cost of revenues from the services reorganization of $4.2 million, impairment costs relating to the software-focused businesses reorganization of $7.1 million, and cost of revenues from other reorganization-related costs of $2.4 million), compared to 29.9% in the corresponding period a year ago. The year-to-date gross margin on adjusted revenues excluding adjusting items decreased primarily due to the impact on margin of lower revenues, partially offset by program mix including the impact of increased higher-margin after-sales service revenues.\nSelling, general and administrative expenses. SG&A expenses for the second quarter of fiscal 2027 were $144.6 million and included $14.0 million of costs related to the amortization of identifiable intangible assets on business acquisitions, $0.1 million of incremental costs related to the Company's acquisition activity, $1.4 million of CEO inducement costs, and $0.3 million related to other reorganization-related costs. Excluding these items, SG&A expenses were $128.8 million in the second quarter of fiscal 2027. Comparably, SG&A expenses for the second quarter of fiscal 2026 were $134.5 million, which excluded $14.8 million of costs related to the amortization of identifiable intangible assets on business acquisitions, and $0.1 million of incremental costs related to the Company's acquisition activity. Lower SG&A expenses in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 primarily reflected the impact of lower employee costs. The CEO inducement costs are recognized over the term of the award, which will be paid April 1, 2027.\n12\n"}
