ompensation revaluation expenses, in addition to a $7.3 million reversal of previously recorded stock-based compensation expense due to the departure of the Company's former CEO.\nFor the six months ended September 27, 2026, stock-based compensation expense was $6.4 million, which included a $2.8 million recovery of stock-based compensation revaluation expenses. This is compared to a stock-based compensation expense of $1.7 million a year earlier, which included a $0.1 million recovery of stock-based compensation revaluation expenses, in addition to a $7.3 million reversal of previously recorded stock-based compensation expense due to the departure of the Company's former CEO.\n13\nEarnings and adjusted earnings from operations (in millions of dollars)\nThree Months Ended\nSeptember 27, 2026 Three Months Ended\nSeptember 28, 2025 Six Months Ended\nSeptember 27, 2026 Six Months Ended\nSeptember 28, 2025\nEarnings from operations $ 23.2 $ 75.2 $ 47.4 $ 133.0\n"}
